<h2>Tips for Best Results</h2>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Zoom in on thumbnails:</strong> If page content is too small to read in the preview, use your browser zoom (Ctrl/Cmd + +) to enlarge thumbnails.</li>
  <li><strong>Check first page:</strong> Make sure the first page is indeed a cover or content you want. Sometimes PDFs have hidden metadata pages.</li>
  <li><strong>Extract a test:</strong> Before extracting many pages, try extracting 2–3 to verify it works as expected.</li>
  <li><strong>Name your downloads:</strong> Your extracted PDF downloads as "extracted-pages.pdf" — rename it immediately if you're extracting multiple files to avoid confusion.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Troubleshooting</h2>

<h3>Thumbnails Not Loading</h3>
<p>
  Large PDFs (100+ MB) may take a moment to render thumbnails. Wait 10–15 seconds. If thumbnails still don't appear, try a smaller PDF first to test.
</p>

<h3>Selected Pages Don't Appear in Order</h3>
<p>
  This is a display quirk. Click pages in the order you want them in the extracted PDF. The result will match your click sequence even if the page numbers are out of order.
</p>

<h3>Downloaded PDF Is Corrupted</h3>
<p>
  This is rare, but if it happens: try extracting fewer pages at once (e.g., 10 pages instead of 50), or try the <a href="/pdfwonder/pdf-splitter/">PDF Splitter tool</a> instead, which uses a different extraction method.
</p>

